## What NOT To Do

- Do NOT create new UI components — the existing components in `/components` are complete. Only modify them to swap localStorage → dbService and geminiService → apiClient.
- Do NOT change any visual styling, layout, or component structure — only data flow changes.
- Do NOT put business logic (calorie calculation, weekly data processing) in API routes — this stays in `utils/dataUtils.ts` on the client.
- Do NOT create new Gemini schema definitions — they already exist in the original `geminiService.ts`. Copy them exactly into `lib/geminiServer.ts`.
- Do NOT add any client-side state management library (Redux, Zustand) — existing React `useState` pattern is correct for this app.
- Do NOT add React Query or SWR — plain `useEffect` + `useState` is the existing pattern.
- Do NOT use `supabase.from().select()` in API routes — API routes use `geminiServer.ts` for AI and `supabaseAdmin` only for rate limiting. All user data queries go through `dbService.ts` on the client.
- Do NOT skip the `requireAuth` call in any API route — every route must validate the JWT.
- Do NOT use `response.json()` in API routes before checking `response.ok` in `apiClient.ts`.

